  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Commission Capacity Building Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Saint Lucia National Commission for UNESCO was established on 2nd February 1981. Since its establishment the National Commission has contributed to the development of Saint Lucia in all of UNESCO&#x2019;s fields of competence. Despite its obvious impact over the years, the need to clarify its roles and functions is as relevant today as it was over 43 years ago. 
It is within this context that this project proposal has been developed. 
The project will seek to provide capacity building and training to members of the National Commission&#x2019;s sub-commissions and committees, as well as assist in revitalizing the Associated Schools Project Network.</narrative>
  </description>
